In Java 17, these GC options are valid (i.e., recognized by the JVM in standard OpenJDK builds):

✅ Common, production collectors

G1GC (default in Java 17)
-XX:+UseG1GC

Parallel GC (Throughput GC)
-XX:+UseParallelGC

Serial GC (single-threaded, small heaps)
-XX:+UseSerialGC

✅ Low-latency collectors (also valid in Java 17)

ZGC (concurrent, low pause)
-XX:+UseZGC

Shenandoah (concurrent, low pause)
-XX:+UseShenandoahGC
Note: Available in many OpenJDK distributions; some vendor builds may omit it, but if your JVM supports it, this flag is valid.

✅ Special-purpose

Epsilon GC (no-op GC; for testing)
-XX:+UseEpsilonGC

❌ Not valid in Java 17

CMS (Concurrent Mark Sweep) — removed (you’ll get “Unrecognized VM option”)
-XX:+UseConcMarkSweepGC ❌